\ cv8-fuse-inline.4 - a short colon definition copied in place of its call, in code compiled at RUN time (Iteration
\ 694: the gene rtinline; step 3 of results/drafts/search-reopen-plan-677.md, mechanism 2 - relf's inlining, at its
\ 3 instructions and 6 bytes). Loaded after cv8-fuse-var.4 and before cv8-fuse-const.4 (a constant stays its literal,
\ for rtimm), for either family, and only for designs with the gene.
\
\ A call to a word whose body, to its EXIT, is at most three instructions in six bytes, every one of them an operation
\ that does not depend on where it sits, becomes a copy of those bytes: one dispatch less for the call and one for the
\ EXIT. Copied as they are, so a call, a branch, a loop operation, the return stack's and the locals' operations are
\ never in it - INL-OPS's whitelist (tools/layout.py writes it, in this design's codes). A body whose last operation
\ has the EXIT folded into it is copied with that operation's plain code. Under the two-bit tag with the JIT a word
\ begins with the JIT's header, stepped over.

CREATE INL-OPS ( --- c-addr )   HERE 152 ALLOT 152 0 FILL
\ [0-63] two bits for each one-byte code: 0 not copied, else its length with its operand (1-3); [64-95] a bit for each
\ code with the EXIT folded in whose plain form is copied (695: the pairs searched only for those - the search for
\ every call compiled cost the corpus workload 12 %); [96] the JIT's code, [97] the length of its header (0: none);
\ [98] a count, then that many pairs: a code with the EXIT folded in, the same operation's code without it. All
\ zeros: nothing copied. (696: a bitmap of the codes a body can begin with, to pass over the rest at once, bought
\ nothing measurable - the scan's cost is in words that begin with a copied operation - results/rehearsal-696.md.)
ALIGN

VARIABLE INL-A ( --- a-addr )   \ the body's first byte
VARIABLE INL-U ( --- a-addr )   \ its length to the EXIT
VARIABLE INL-L ( --- a-addr )   \ where in it the last instruction begins
VARIABLE INL-F ( --- a-addr )   \ 0, or 256 + the plain code of a last instruction that folded the EXIT in (a code can be 0)

: INL-LEN ( c --- n )   DUP 2 RSHIFT INL-OPS + C@ SWAP 3 AND 2* RSHIFT 3 AND ;

: INL-UNFOLD ( c --- c2 -1 | 0 )
  DUP 3 RSHIFT INL-OPS 64 + + C@ OVER 7 AND RSHIFT 1 AND 0= IF DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  INL-OPS 98 + C@ 0 ?DO
    DUP INL-OPS 99 + I 2* + C@ = IF DROP INL-OPS 100 + I 2* + C@ -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
  LOOP DROP 0 ;

: INL-BODY ( xt --- flag )
\ True if xt's body can be copied: INL-A, INL-U, INL-L and INL-F describe it.
  DUP C@ INL-OPS 96 + C@ = INL-OPS 97 + C@ AND ?DUP IF + THEN
  INL-A ! 0 INL-U ! 0 INL-F !
  4 0 DO
    INL-A @ INL-U @ + C@
    DUP EXIT-OP = IF DROP -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
    I 3 = IF DROP 0 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
    INL-U @ INL-L !
    DUP INL-UNFOLD IF SWAP DROP DUP 256 OR INL-F ! THEN
    INL-LEN ?DUP 0= IF 0 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
    INL-U +!  INL-U @ 6 > IF 0 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
    INL-F @ IF -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
  LOOP 0 ;

: INL, ( --- )
\ Lay the body INL-BODY found.
  HERE INL-U @ 0 ?DO INL-A @ I + C@ C, LOOP                ( start )
  INL-F @ IF INL-F @ 255 AND OVER INL-L @ + C! THEN
  INL-L @ +  INL-U @ IF DUP C@ INL-LEN 1 = IF LAST-OP ! EXIT THEN THEN  DROP 0 LAST-OP ! ;

: COMPILE,8 ( xt --- )
\ The COMPILE,8 before this one, with a call to a short body laid as the body.
  DUP PRIMITIVE? 0= IF DUP INL-BODY IF DROP INL, EXIT THEN THEN COMPILE,8 ;
